WEBVTT

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:12.580
Now that the first trimester of our
first year in high school is over,

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:14.190
we're on summer vacation.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.030
I'm so burned out!

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:22.700
I heard the stories, but summers
in Kyoto are way hotter than I thought...

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:27.040
What are you talking about, Aya?
It's going to get a lot hotter.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.790
What?! No!

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:36.080
I know! The sea! Let's go to the beach
together and wash away the heat!

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:39.330
Sure, but Kyoto isn't near the ocean.

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:40.750
Really?

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.500
Yeah, it might be a bit tough to visit
and come back in one day.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.290
In that case, we can stay overnight!

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:51.160
You say that like it's easy,
but it'll cost a lot of money.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:52.250
Are you sure?

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:54.830
Well... um...

00:00:54.830 --> 00:01:00.450
But I can't just not go to the beach
during summer vacation. That's sad...

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.700
Um... in that case...

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.620
Okay, I'm off.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:13.410
Be careful out there.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:14.950
Okay!

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:21.950
So Aya-chan, Midori-chan, and I have
decided to go on a trip together.

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:23.680
Destination: Kanazawa.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.220
My Aunt Miyabi runs an inn out there.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:34.150
Miki going out on
a trip with her friends...

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:36.940
Is she going to be okay?

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:44.860
Please take good care
of Miki and her friends.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:25.000
I'm so glad the weather is so nice!

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.620
Wow, we really went on
a trip, just the three of us.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.580
I've never been to Kanazawa!

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:31.120
To tell you the truth, me neither.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:35.250
We're so lucky that
Miki-chan's aunt runs an inn!

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:36.620
Yes.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:38.160
The beach is close to the inn,

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.200
and she said we can stay for
a few days in a vacant room.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:47.400
Oh, Miki-chan! Friendship
is such a precious thing!

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.910
Is your aunt's inn nearby?

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:53.160
No, it's about 30 minutes
from here by train.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:56.620
In that case, let's go sightseeing
before we go to the inn!

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:58.370
Huh? You don't want to go to the beach?

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:02.790
Let's go! We're staying two nights,
we can go to the beach tomorrow.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:05.700
Yes! Now that we're here,
I want to see lots of stuff!

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.750
This area looks so promising!

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:10.540
Sure. If you're okay
with that, let's do that.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:15.080
All right, let's go sightseeing in Kanazawa!

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:16.700
Yeah!

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:34.500
Wow, that was fun! We saw so much stuff!

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.120
Want to head to the inn now?

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:41.450
Sure. I told Aunt Miyabi that
we'd be there in the evening.

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:43.290
I'm so excited about dinner!

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:46.160
Aya, you're literally eating
ice cream right now.

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:50.250
It'll be fine! I'm sure I'll be
hungry by the time we get there!

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.540
Well, hello, girls!

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:55.910
Thank you for coming all
the way from Kyoto.

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:58.200
Hi, Aunt Miyabi, long time no see.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:04.250
Indeed! I'll let your mother know
you arrived safely. She was worried.

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:06.040
Oh, she was?

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:08.250
And are these your friends?

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:12.370
Thank you for your hospitality.
I am Ono Midori, Miki-san's classmate.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:15.080
I'm Takayashiki Aya, also from her class.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:21.580
Oh, how polite of you.
Well, come in, come in. Dinner is ready.

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:29.330
Wow! This looks delicious!

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:30.720
Enjoy.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:35.580
Are you sure? We aren't even paying...

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:39.120
Don't worry. You're Miki's friends.

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:43.040
I should be a great host,
or my sister would be angry!

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:45.080
Thank you, Aunt Miyabi.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:47.160
You're welcome.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:49.450
Well, taking you up on the generous offer...

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:51.580
Let's eat!

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.870
Mm! Delicious!

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:01.200
This is the best sashimi I've ever had!

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:04.120
I guess this must be
because the ocean is so close.

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:09.370
What is it? You look very happy.

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:15.330
Well, you used to be so shy and scared
of people, but now you have great friends.

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:17.450
I'm so happy...

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:21.200
She can be difficult,
but please be nice to her.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.910
H-Hey! Auntie!

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:25.950
Oh, we're super close already!

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:27.250
Yes.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:35.000
The bath is ready, too, whenever
you like. Please take your time.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.290
Yes!

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:37.450
Thank you very much!

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:42.330
Wow! That was super good!

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:47.500
Kanazawa is really great. The city
is very tasteful and the food is great.

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.330
This place is my new favorite!

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:51.420
Midori-chan, you sound like an old lady.

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:54.410
Aya! Who are you calling old lady?!

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:55.500
Whoa!

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:58.120
Ouch!

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:02.160
Oh!

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.830
Oh, no!

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:11.040
Wait, what's wrong with these pieces?
There's nothing on the back side.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:11.790
Huh?

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:13.660
See, look.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:16.040
You're right. It's blank on the back.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:20.370
Right? Shogi pieces are supposed
to have characters on the back, too, right?

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:24.200
Like Dragon behind the Rook
and Gold behind the Silver.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.250
These aren't Shogi pieces.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:27.370
Huh...?

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:29.950
I think... they might be <i>GOITA</i> pieces.

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:30.950
<i>GOITA?</i>

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.830
What's that, Midori-chan?

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:37.660
It's a traditional game from a port town
named Ushitsu, on the Noto peninsula.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:41.330
Oh, you know about <i>GOITA?</i>

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:44.700
I'm impressed that you know that
game despite being from Kyoto.

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:47.870
Midori-chan works at a board game store,

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:50.080
and she knows a lot
about all sorts of games.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:52.160
Oh, is that so!

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:56.580
<i>GOITA</i> 's unique rules caught the attention
of some game researchers a while ago.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:08:00.580
They've turned it into a card game.
We sell it in our store, too.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:03.870
I'm ashamed to admit that
I haven't played it yet.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:07.790
I've never seen a proper <i>GOITA</i>
set made of bamboo before.

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:09.750
Is it okay if I studied this?

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:11.830
Yes, of course.

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:15.000
Hey, Midori-chan, can we try it out?

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:18.290
Sure, but we need
four players to play <i>GOITA</i> .

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:20.040
Wait, four?

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.000
One...

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:21.950
...two...

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:23.000
...three...

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:24.000
...four.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:24.830
Oh?

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:27.250
Wait, why are you including the landlady?

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:29.160
Well, you know.

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:33.040
Sure, sure. I'm not busy at the moment.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:33.870
Are you sure?

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:35.620
Yay!

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:39.580
Um...

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:41.870
I match your Bishop and play a Gold.

00:08:41.870 --> 00:08:43.750
I can't play anything!

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:45.870
There, I win.

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:47.870
Impressive!

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:52.950
I lost! This is hard!

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:58.160
This game is super fun!
I wish I'd played this sooner!

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:02.870
Seriously. I didn't know such
a fun game existed out here.

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:05.040
Oh? It's not your first time.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:05.950
Huh?

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:10.370
Miki, you've played this
game when you were little.

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:12.540
I did...?

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:18.370
Hmm... I get the feeling that she's right,
but I don't remember at all...

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.240
It's fine if you can't remember.

00:09:23.030 --> 00:09:24.950
Ba

00:09:23.030 --> 00:09:24.950
th

00:09:23.030 --> 00:09:24.950
Women's 
bath

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:28.540
What a great bath!

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:30.540
<i>GOITA</i> was fun!

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:34.410
Why was such a fun game
exclusive to the Noto area?

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:37.660
Similar games were played
all over Japan, actually.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:38.500
Huh?

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:39.620
Really?

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:46.830
Like, <i>Maru-Shogi</i> and <i>Imo-Shogi</i> are
basically the same game using Shogi pieces.

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:49.620
<i>Iro-Kammuri</i> is a very similar game
that uses <i>Hyakunin Isshu</i> cards,

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:53.540
you just play to a different hand size.

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:58.790
Apparently, these games
were often used for gambling.

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:02.750
Starting in the Edo era, numerous bans
on gambling were put into law.

00:10:02.750 --> 00:10:04.620
The games went out
of popularity after that.

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:06.200
I see.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.410
Knowledgeable as always, Midori-chan.

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:13.620
So that's why <i>GOITA</i> only remained
in just a part of the Noto region.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:15.750
I want to play again.

00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:17.250
Yes.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:20.830
Okay, I'm turning the light off.

00:10:22.790 --> 00:10:24.410
Tomorrow's the beach, finally!

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:26.950
You're so excited about it.

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:34.950
Yes... So excited that...
I might have trouble falling asleep...

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:38.900
Aya-chan...?

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:42.250
Wow... She's asleep already.

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:43.500
Huh?

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:48.700
Look at her, so happy-looking...
I envy her personality.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:52.040
Hey, come on, Midori-chan.

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:56.950
She must have been tired.
Goodnight, Aya-chan.

00:10:56.950 --> 00:10:59.160
Okay, we should get to sleep, too.

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:00.790
Yes.

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:05.330
Miki, thanks.

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:06.540
Huh?

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:12.950
I never dreamed of going on such
a luxurious trip. It's all thanks to you.

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:15.450
Oh, no...

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:17.910
It's me who needs to thank you.

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:19.000
Huh?

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:23.620
If I didn't meet you, I wouldn't
have been introduced to games either.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:28.080
I would have lived my life not knowing
there was so much fun to be had.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:30.620
Thank you, Midori-chan.

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:33.500
Miki...

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:39.200
Let's play... lots... together...

00:11:40.660 --> 00:11:42.700
Miki...

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:45.670
Oh, no... Now I'm losing sleep...

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:52.010
{Between}

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:54.830
Hurry! Hurry!

00:11:56.450 --> 00:11:59.580
What are you doing, you two?
It's the beach! The beach!

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:03.370
You're way too excited, Aya!
Did you put on sunscreen?

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:05.120
I can do that later!

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:06.830
It's pointless to do it later!

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:10.160
Aya-chan, you don't have to rush;
the ocean isn't going anywhere.

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:13.580
I know, but hurry!

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:15.580
Off we go!

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:17.950
Huh?

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:28.910
How can this be?! It was so sunny
just moments ago! It's not fair!

00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:32.250
Just accept it already.
There's nothing we can do.

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:33.120
No!

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:34.430
No!

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:37.410
Beach!

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:40.910
Come on, we can't change the weather...

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:42.500
No!

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:46.450
You said we're going!

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:48.160
You know...

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:49.820
What should we do, Midori-chan?

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:55.080
What choice do we... Oh, wait.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:56.410
We can play this.

00:12:56.410 --> 00:12:57.660
Good idea!

00:12:57.660 --> 00:12:58.330
Real nice.

00:12:58.330 --> 00:12:59.410
What are you doing?

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:02.370
Oh, this boy...

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:03.750
Hello!

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:06.750
This is a game called <i>GOITA</i> .

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:09.330
Do you want to join us?

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:10.290
Yes!

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:14.500
Come on, Takashi.
Don't bother the young ladies.

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:15.950
Come here!

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:18.950
No! I'm playing a game!

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:20.830
Stop being selfish!

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:25.330
It's okay, sir. We actually need
four players to play this game.

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:28.370
Yes! So it'd be super
helpful if he joined us!

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:31.500
See, Dad? Listen to them!

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:33.040
Are you sure it's all right?

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:38.160
Yes, given the weather,
we're stuck in the inn anyway, so...

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:39.500
Let's play together.

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:40.870
Yeah!

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:45.160
Well, I will take you up
on your offer then.

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:48.250
So let me explain the rules of <i>GOITA</i> .

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:51.910
<i>GOITA</i> is played by
two teams of two players each.

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:57.040
There are 32 pieces total.
Two Kings, two Rooks, two Bishops...

00:13:57.040 --> 00:14:01.160
...four Golds, Silvers, Knights, and Lances...

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:03.700
...and ten Pawns.

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:05.370
Wow!

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:10.410
We turn these all facedown,
and take eight each to play.

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:12.000
Here are the rules:

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:18.910
The dealer puts one piece facedown,
then another piece faceup.

00:14:18.910 --> 00:14:21.200
This second piece is the "attack."

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:26.370
The next player can "match" this
by playing the same piece, if they have it.

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:34.830
If you successfully match, you become
the dealer and play another attack.

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:41.660
You repeat this process until one player
plays all eight pieces in their hand.

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:42.810
That player's team wins.

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:46.600
The last piece you play determines
your score for that round.

00:14:47.730 --> 00:14:52.860
You play several rounds, and the team
to first score 150 points total wins.

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:58.540
Also, if the last move you play is two
of the same tiles, you get double the points.

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:00.160
Wow! Double!

00:15:00.910 --> 00:15:03.200
Here are some more special rules:

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:05.080
The King is special and can
match five different pieces:

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:13.950
The Rook, Bishop, Gold, Silver, and Knight.
So basically, just not the Lance and Pawn.

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:16.500
However, you cannot play
the King as an attack piece

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.830
until someone first plays it as a match piece.

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:19.870
I get it!

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:23.330
Those are the rules, pretty much.
Do you understand?

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:25.000
Yep! I got it!

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:26.830
Okay, let's make teams!

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:30.000
Since it's your first game, maybe
Takashi-kun can pair up with Midori-chan?

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.700
She's really good at games!

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:34.370
Good luck, Takashi-kun.

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:35.750
Okay!

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:37.620
Okay, you can start.

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:39.120
Got it!

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:44.620
Well... So I play the
first piece facedown...

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:47.700
...and I attack with Gold!

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:51.330
I will match your Gold
and attack with Silver.

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:53.370
I will match your Silver
and play a Knight.

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:56.950
Matching your Knight,
attacking with Rook...

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:08.620
I'll have two Pawns left over,
but this is the turning point!

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:12.660
Match your Gold, attack with Bishop!

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:13.500
I pass...

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:14.660
All right!

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:15.280
Huh...?

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:17.820
Match the Bishop and attack with Silver!

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:19.500
Oh...

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:21.120
Yes!

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:24.080
Match your Silver and finish with a Pawn!

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:25.620
Ten points!

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:28.830
Oh, no! We lost!

00:16:28.830 --> 00:16:31.080
If you let the Bishop through,
I would have had to pass.

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:32.950
Wait, really?

00:16:32.950 --> 00:16:36.170
Takashi-kun, you weren't
supposed to play that Bishop.

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:37.910
Huh? Why?

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:42.410
You win if your teammate wins.
So there's no need to interfere with me.

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:46.120
Don't match your partner's attack.
That's the basic strategy.

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:50.200
Oh, I get it!
Don't match my teammate's attack.

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:52.540
Got it! I'll do better next time!

00:16:56.950 --> 00:16:59.120
Match with King! Go Rook!

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:05.620
She matched my Silver with a King,
so she probably doesn't have any Silvers...

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:07.250
Match with King, and play Silver.

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:10.250
I pass...

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:16.500
Miki doesn't have one either. That must
mean Takashi-kun has all the Silvers!

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:19.200
Hmm. I pass, too.

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:20.700
What...?!

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:25.540
Okay, I play another facedown
and finish with Rook, 40 points.

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:29.750
That's 150 points! Miki-chan and I win!

00:17:29.750 --> 00:17:33.370
Oh, no, we lost!

00:17:33.370 --> 00:17:38.530
Takashi-kun, if you had two Silvers back
then, you could have matched them.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.120
Then you would have won...

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:45.370
What? But earlier, you said
I shouldn't match my teammate's moves.

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:49.700
That's the basic strategy,
but this was special.

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:52.330
If you paid attention
to the pieces, you would know.

00:17:52.330 --> 00:17:53.750
Huh?

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:57.080
I remember now...

00:17:57.080 --> 00:18:03.910
Why didn't you match my Gold? Then you
would have won since you have two Golds!

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:06.830
But you said I can't match
my teammate's attack...

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:11.290
That was different! Why don't you get it?

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:13.450
I'm sorry... I don't understand...

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:16.370
I can't play this game...

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:19.830
Hey, Miki! Miki-chan!

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:24.860
Takashi-kun is in the same spot
that I was in back then...

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:30.950
So am I supposed to match
or not...? I don't get it...

00:18:30.950 --> 00:18:31.790
Takashi-kun.

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:37.210
You want to tag with me next?
Let's play on the same team.

00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:39.370
Okay.

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:43.290
Hmm?

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:49.500
Match with a Lance
and attack with a Silver!

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:52.410
Match with a Silver
and attack with a Knight.

00:18:52.410 --> 00:18:53.450
Pass.

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:55.290
Um... pass.

00:18:55.290 --> 00:19:00.290
Bah! Fine! I have a King! And Rook!

00:19:00.290 --> 00:19:04.860
Aya-chan probably doesn't have
a Knight... What about Midori-chan...?

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:10.870
I have to take a risk.

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:13.830
Match with a King, and attack with Knight!

00:19:15.910 --> 00:19:17.330
I pass.

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:20.580
Midori-chan doesn't have a Knight either.

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:24.370
So both of the remaining Knights must be...

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:25.590
...Takashi-kun's.

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:32.790
Two Kings already played...
Miki-nee-chan played two Knights...

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:35.830
I have both of the Knights left!

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:43.150
Miki-nee-chan...?

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:50.660
Match with a Knight,
and attack with Knight!

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:55.580
This is the right play, right, Miki-nee-chan?

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:05.870
He got it! He understood my intent!

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:07.680
Good move, Takashi-kun!

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:09.870
Pass!

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:10.550
I pass!

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:11.510
Oh, yeah!

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:13.660
Then it's my turn!

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:18.330
I play this facedown,
then finish with a Lance!

00:20:18.330 --> 00:20:20.040
We won!

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:24.200
Oh, no! We lost! Awesome job, Takashi-kun!

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:26.700
Yes, truly.

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:28.570
We did it, Miki-nee-chan!

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:29.790
Yes!

00:20:37.410 --> 00:20:43.120
Wow, that was fun!
Thanks for playing with me!

00:20:43.120 --> 00:20:45.910
Thank you very much, all of you.

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:49.370
Thanks to you, we now have
a great memory of this trip.

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:50.750
The pleasure is ours.

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:51.750
Yes!

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:54.700
What are your plans
for the rest of the day?

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:57.750
Well, we haven't decided on anything...

00:20:57.750 --> 00:20:59.580
What about the beach?!

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:01.700
Let's go to the beach together!

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:04.160
We can't do that, not in this rain...

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:06.080
The rain's stopped!

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:07.160
Huh?

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:14.660
Wow!

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:16.750
Beach!

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:18.410
I guess it was just a passing shower.

00:21:18.410 --> 00:21:22.290
It looks like we'll have clear skies
for the rest of the afternoon!

00:21:22.290 --> 00:21:24.000
Yes!

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:25.620
Let's go, Takashi-kun!

00:21:25.620 --> 00:21:26.830
Yeah!

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:31.790
Hey, wait! I have to
reapply the sunscreen!

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:34.160
I said that can wait till later!

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.250
It can't!

00:21:39.410 --> 00:21:45.580
Miki really has changed...
It's probably thanks to those two.

00:21:47.040 --> 00:21:49.700
Hey, Aunt Miyabi!

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:52.000
It's great out here!

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:57.790
Tomoe, it seems like your
daughter found a real treasure.

00:21:57.790 --> 00:21:59.750
Oh, my!

00:23:37.500 --> 00:23:40.180
You want to play the game I made?

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:42.510
No! It's not even done yet!

00:23:43.180 --> 00:23:46.520
Wait, what do you mean
it'll never be finished that way...?
